config LED_STRIP_CACHE
	bool "LED strip cache driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_LED_STRIP_CACHE_ENABLED
	help
	  Enable this driver to support a virtual LED device bridging the LED
	  and LED strip APIs. The driver provides a cache for one or more LED
	  strip devices.

config LED_STRIP_CACHE_UPDATE_ALL
	bool "Update all LEDs on each update"
	default n
	depends on LED_STRIP_CACHE
	help
	  Always update all LEDs of a strip instead of stopping at the targeted
	  LED.

	  By default, the LED strip cache driver updates a strip only up to the
	  targeted LED. But some backend controllers may be unable to keep the
	  signal low after a transmission. A high signal at the end of the
	  transmission may be interpreted as an additional bit by the next LED,
	  which can affect its state. In that case you may try to enable this
	  option.
